// Khronos Sponza, referenced straight off the CDN — ~50 MB on first load, nothing committed here.
// The url is absolute, so the vite plugin leaves it alone and both the browser and the Node baker
// fetch it themselves.
//
// One directional light and nothing else: no ambient, no fill, and no shadow map either. Realtime that
// means a flat sun that lights every surface facing it, walls included — the occlusion only exists in
// the bake, which is the whole comparison.
//
// The shadowed courtyard lands ~78x under the sunlit floor here, and the arcades further still, so the
// demo gives this scene its own exposure and tone curve. Nothing is wrong with the atlas at that depth;
// a filmic toe just buries it.

--sun: #fff1d0;

@bakery {
  out: "../public/lightmaps";
  size: 2048;
  samples: 1024;
}

directionalLight #sun(var(--sun), 4) {
  position: vec3(-8, 20, 4);
  // to the baker this is the sun's angular radius in radians — 0.02 rad is a slightly soft disc
  @bakery { radius: 0.02 };
}

gltf #sponza("https://raw.githubusercontent.com/KhronosGroup/glTF-Sample-Assets/main/Models/Sponza/glTF/Sponza.gltf") {}
